35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The yard scanners are a mess of old models. The 2021 trial was ringed with spreadsheets in a month. We need something that works with what we have.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The renewal invoices show bundled deals held price, but separate add-ons climbed yearly. The board minutes show capital gets trimmed, but operating lines pass easily.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Last winter's outage sat unowned for two days. Four suppliers pointed at each other. And the warehouse rules were rewritten twice mid-year. Scope freezes are fiction.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,The 2018 pay move had mismatched route codes for a year. The dispatch tool skipped three upgrades because testing took weeks we didn't have. We age in place.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,Two of four administrators retire this year. The last posting stayed open eleven months. And the last rollout's training was dropped in two depots within weeks.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, if add-ons climb yearly, we are bleeding money. But if the yard devices can't talk to the new system, we bleed time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, time is money. The board minutes confirm we are locked into operating costs. We need a vendor who doesn't nickel-and-dime us.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, the unowned outage is terrifying. We need a single point of accountability. Modular systems might scatter support even more.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I agree. The dispatch tool history shows we can't handle complex upgrades. We need something simple or something that handles the complexity for us.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the yard is critical, but the people are the bottleneck. If we can't hire admins, we can't run a complex system.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, you're right. We can't hire fast enough. We need a system that doesn't require deep admin skills to keep running.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, a single point of accountability is key. But if it's a subscription, we are locked in. We need to see if the price stays flat.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, flat price is good, but if the scope changes, we are stuck. The warehouse rule changes prove we can't freeze scope.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, the training drop-off is a red flag. We need a vendor who stays with us, not just a manual.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, exactly. The depot supervisors shaped their own routines. We need a partner who respects that, not one who imposes rigid steps.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I am leaning towards a system that works with our existing yard devices. A modular approach might let us keep the scanners we have.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,I am worried about the long-term cost. A subscription with a marketplace might hide costs in add-ons. We need transparency.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am concerned about support ownership. A single vendor with a regional team might be better than scattered suppliers.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I am worried about the data lift. We need a vendor who has done this before and can handle the mess.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,I am worried about the people. We need a vendor who will train our remaining staff and stay through the rollout.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
