60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,The candidates are here. A is a cloud suite with a partner for migration. B is modular. C is on-premise with an engineering team. D is a hosted suite with a regional team.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, A's marketplace sounds like a trap for add-on costs. B's separate licenses might climb yearly. C is a one-time purchase, but who maintains it?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, C's engineering team present through rollout addresses the support gap. But if they leave, who is in charge? D's regional team might be more stable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, C's on-premise deployment might be easier to upgrade if we have the team. But our dispatch tool history shows we struggle with upgrades.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, C's engineering team staying through rollout is crucial. Our admins are retiring. We need hands-on help, not just a manual.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, C's on-premise setup might work with our old yard devices. But if the engineering team leaves, we are stuck.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, the five-year invoice data shows separate licenses climb. B is risky. A's subscription might be stable, but the marketplace is a wildcard.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, A's partner firm handling migration is a risk. Last winter's outage showed scattered support fails. We need one throat to choke.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, D's fixed configuration process might avoid the scope creep we saw in the warehouse rules. But is it flexible enough for our depots?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, D's regional service team might be better for training. Our depot supervisors dropped the last rollout's training. We need local support.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, D's fixed configuration might be too rigid. Our yard devices are a mix. We need flexibility. C's on-premise might be more adaptable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, C's one-time purchase is attractive, but the maintenance costs are hidden. The board minutes show operating lines pass easily. We might get stuck with high maintenance.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, C's engineering team present through rollout is a strong point. It addresses the support ownership issue. But what happens after?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, the 2018 pay move shows data lifts are messy. C's engineering team might handle that better than an external partner.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, C's team staying through rollout is vital. Our admins are retiring. We need them to teach the remaining staff.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I am leaning towards C. It works with our existing infrastructure and has a team on-site.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I am worried about C's long-term costs. But the one-time purchase is better than climbing add-ons.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I am concerned about C's post-rollout support. But the engineering team during rollout is a strong plus.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,I am worried about C's upgrade path. But the on-premise setup might be easier to manage.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,I am leaning towards C. The engineering team staying through rollout is exactly what we need for our retiring admins.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
